implementationPlan.description:
Host import: new scripts/local-runner/snapshot-import.mjs exporting importCandidate, plus host test rows X4-X6.

Read first: the landed CQ-R09c module scripts/local-runner/snapshot-transfer.mjs (snapshotArgv, assertNoMounts, runSupervisorStream and its onFrame error propagation, and its TRANSFER_* codes), the fake provider in its host test rows, and the isCanonicalBase64 rule in scripts/local-runner/guest-bridge.mjs. Reuse them and do not edit R09c's module.

importCandidate({ name, provider = {}, timeoutMs }):
- Header comment: every guest byte is untrusted. Frames carry no identity; size, sha256 and digest come only from validateImport over the transferred bytes (DoD 2). This is local transfer logic, not isolation certification, and executionReady stays false.
- Input validation happens before any provider call. An invalid name, provider or timeoutMs rejects with a fixed IMPORT_INPUT_INVALID, or with R09c's own input code where its helpers validate.
- assertNoMounts(name, provider) runs before spawning, so a refusal never spawns. It runs again after the stream ends (DoD 3).
- Call runSupervisorStream({ name, mode: 'export', provider, timeoutMs, input: [], onFrame }). onFrame is a strict state machine over exact-key plain objects:
  - {kind:'file', path, executable, size}: path a string, executable a boolean, size a safe integer >= 0. It opens a file.
  - {kind:'data', data}: allowed only inside an open file. data must be canonical, non-empty base64 (Buffer round trip), and the decoded bytes may not pass the file's size. A file closes when its bytes reach size exactly; an empty file closes at once.
  - {kind:'delete', path}, {kind:'symlink', path} and {kind:'special', path}: allowed only when no file is open.
  - {kind:'end', entries}: entries must equal the entries received, no file may be open, and no frame may follow.
  Anything else throws a fixed IMPORT_PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, including an extra key such as sha256, oid or digest. A stream that ends without its end frame does too.
- Bounds are checked at each header, before any data is buffered: more than MAX_IMPORT_ENTRIES entries, or more than MAX_IMPORT_BYTES of declared file bytes, throws snapshotError('SNAPSHOT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED').
- Entries become R09a input exactly:
  - file -> {kind:'file', path, executable, data: Buffer.concat(chunks)};
  - delete -> {kind:'delete', path};
  - symlink -> {kind:'symlink', path};
  - special -> {kind:'special', path}.
- validateImport(entries) is the ONLY admission gate, so its codes surface unchanged:
  - SNAPSHOT_SYMLINK_DENIED for a symlink;
  - SNAPSHOT_ENTRY_INVALID for a special file;
  - SNAPSHOT_PATH_INVALID for traversal, absolute, backslash or non-portable paths;
  - SNAPSHOT_CONTROL_PATH for .git, .moe and the other control segments, at any depth and in any case;
  - SNAPSHOT_PATH_COLLISION.
  Do not re-implement any of those rules here.
- Resolves Object.freeze({ instance: name, candidate, executionReady: false }), where candidate is validateImport's frozen result. It never returns a partial candidate, and a refusal leaves nothing behind.

Error handling: one fixed-text error helper like snapshotError or bridgeError. No guest text, path or byte appears in any message, and every rejection path kills the provider through runSupervisorStream.

Host test rows X4-X6 go in the CQ-R09 section of scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs. They use a fake provider:
- a fakeGuest-style run for info and the mountinfo probe;
- a spawn whose child replays scripted guest frames, length-prefixed like encodeFrame;
- a kill() that emits 'close' asynchronously (setImmediate), as Node does. A synchronous close masks the kill path (gotcha from R08's H-rows).
Build each hostile stream so exactly one rule fails, so that no missing check can hide behind another.

Rows:
- X4 A clean stream resolves a candidate whose entries, sizes, sha256 values and digest deepEqual validateImport of the same entries built in the test. The recorded provider calls are exactly: info, the mountinfo probe, snapshotArgv(name, 'export') spawned with shell:false and no extra argv, then info and mountinfo again. Mounts present or unknown before the stream refuse it with no spawn, and mounts present after it refuse it too.
- X5 Hostile but well-formed streams are refused with the R09a code and no candidate: '../x', '/abs', 'a/../b', a backslash path ('a\\b'), '.git/config', '.moe/x', 'sub/.Claude/settings.json', 'GIT~1/config', a symlink entry, a special entry, case-folded duplicates ('A' and 'a'), and an ancestor collision ('a' and 'a/b').
- X6 Each protocol violation gives its fixed code and kills the provider:
  - a file header with an extra sha256 or oid key;
  - data before any header, or data past size;
  - a stream ending mid-file;
  - non-canonical base64;
  - an end count mismatch, a missing end, or a frame after end;
  - a count over MAX_IMPORT_ENTRIES, or a declared size over MAX_IMPORT_BYTES, refused before any data frame is read;
  - a nonzero provider exit;
  - a provider that never exits (timeout).

End-to-end round trip, X7: the real exporter (R09b), transfer (R09c) and supervisor together, proving DoD 1-3 across the whole flow. The row goes in the CQ-R09 section of scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs, skipped on win32 with a reason (POSIX python3), with an async timeout.

Setup:
- Build a temporary Git repo with committed files, including one executable, a nested path and a committed .moe/x control path. Then make a dirty overlay: one modified file, one untracked file and one deleted file.
- exportSourceSnapshot (CQ-R09b) on that repo's HEAD commit gives the snapshot; assert .moe/x is counted in excluded.
- The provider's run is the healthy fakeGuest from this file. Its spawn ignores the multipass argv except the final mode, and runs the real supervisor's materialize() or export() through the python3 -I -B seam with the test's temp workspace and manifest paths, owner = the current uid and gid, and drop=lambda: None.

Round trip:
- materializeSnapshot (CQ-R09c), then importCandidate on the untouched workspace, gives a candidate with zero entries.
- Then act as the agent: edit a file, add a nested file, delete a file and chmod +x a file.
- importCandidate now resolves exactly those four entries, each sha256 equal to sha256 of the bytes written, and .moe/x was never in the workspace.

Attacks, each on a freshly materialized workspace, are each refused with no candidate:
- a planted symlink to /etc/passwd: SNAPSHOT_SYMLINK_DENIED;
- a planted symlink to a host-only temp file: refused the same way, and that file's content must never appear in any frame;
- a written .git/config, and a written .moe/state.json: SNAPSHOT_CONTROL_PATH;
- a file whose name holds a backslash: SNAPSHOT_PATH_INVALID;
- a FIFO: SNAPSHOT_ENTRY_INVALID;
- a mount that appears between materialize and import (the fake info reports one) refuses the import.

Across every X7 run, assert DoD 3:
- each provider call is info, the mountinfo exec probe, or snapshotArgv(name, mode);
- every exec carries --no-map-working-directory;
- no call names mount or transfer.

Test cleanup and error handling: remove every temp repo, workspace and manifest in t.after, leave no python child running, and make a failed assertion kill the spawned seam process.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff only (load the adversarial-self-review skill). Read the diff as each attacker in turn:
- A hostile supervisor: any frame order, a duplicate or missing end, oversized declarations, non-canonical base64, extra identity keys, and paths that collide or traverse.
- A hostile agent in the workspace: swapping a file for a symlink or FIFO between lstat and open, a hardlink, a 100 GB sparse file, chmod 000, a 2,000-deep tree, 10,001 entries, and non-UTF-8 or control-character names.
- The environment: two exports at once on one VM, host EOF, timeouts, and a missing agent account.

Check that:
- the privilege drop precedes every workspace read;
- every fd closes on every path;
- error handling never leaks a path, guest text or byte;
- DoD 1-3 each have a test that fails if its guard is removed. Spot-check by deleting one guard at a time in a scratch copy (git archive into a temp dir), never in the shared tree;
- verified-local and executionReady are unchanged;
- there is no new mount or transfer argv, no .moe edit and no Git write.

Fix anything found with a test, then re-run step 4's command and supply that fresh output to complete_task.
